---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.js';
const sections = [
  ['summary', 'In short'],
  ['collect', 'What we collect'],
  ['hosting', 'Hosting'],
  ['newsletter', 'The newsletter'],
  ['email', 'If you email us'],
  ['links', 'Other websites'],
  ['rights', 'Your rights'],
  ['changes', 'Changes'],
];
---
<Page
  title="Privacy"
  kicker="Your data"
  intro="We collect as little as possible. No cookies, no tracking, no ads following you around. Here’s exactly what happens when you use Aerial."
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="summary">In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We don’t use cookies.</li>
    <li>We don’t use analytics or tracking tools, and we don’t run ads that track you.</li>
    <li>We don’t have accounts or logins, and we don’t sell or share personal data.</li>
    <li>Our fonts and images are hosted on our own site, so reading Aerial doesn’t send your details to Google or other third parties.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This notice explains how {site.controller} (“we”) handle personal data under UK data protection law (the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018). For any privacy question, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Privacy`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
  <p>When you simply read Aerial, we don’t collect anything that identifies you. If you sign up to the newsletter, we store your email address (see below). The gig map filters and quiz run in your browser and nothing is stored or sent to us.</p>

  <h2 id="hosting">Hosting</h2>
  <p>Aerial is hosted by Netlify. Like any web host, Netlify’s servers process technical information when you visit, such as your IP address, browser type and the pages you request. They need this to deliver the site and protect it from attacks. We don’t use this information to identify you. Netlify may process it outside the UK under its own safeguards. See <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" rel="noopener">Netlify’s privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="newsletter">The newsletter</h2>
  <p>When you sign up, we store your email address, the date you signed up and the page you signed up from. We use your email only to send you the newsletter, and we do this because you asked us to (your consent).</p>
  <p>Sign-ups are kept in a Google Sheet in our Google account, so Google stores them on our behalf. Google may process them outside the UK under its own safeguards. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google’s privacy policy</a>. Submitting the form doesn’t send anything to Google from your browser: our site passes your email on.</p>
  <p>Before we send the first issue, we’ll name the service we use to send it here. Every newsletter will let you unsubscribe with one click, and you can also email us to be removed. When you unsubscribe, we delete your email from our list.</p>

  <h2 id="email">If you email us</h2>
  <p>If you email us, for example to pitch a piece, correct venue information or report a problem, we’ll use your email and what you send only to reply and act on it. We delete messages we no longer need, and at the latest after two years.</p>

  <h2 id="links">Other websites</h2>
  <p>We link to ticket sites, venues and other music publications. When you follow a link, that site’s own privacy policy applies. Our share links only open the other service when you click them.</p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to show you any personal data we hold about you, correct it, delete it, or stop using it. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Data%20request`}>{site.email}</a> and we’ll respond within one month.</p>
  <p>If you’re unhappy with how we’ve handled your data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>We’ll update this page whenever what we collect changes, for example when the newsletter launches, and change the date below.</p>
  <p class="updated">Last updated {site.lastReviewed}.</p>
</Page>
